00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Higgins, I know that you
find math boring.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.601
-Yeah.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.601
-Well, that's why I've taken --

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.934
I've updated math
to make the equations

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.734
be about stuff
that you can relate to.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:10.901
-Oh!
-Yeah, it's a new segment

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.200
called "Popular Mathematics."

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.334
Here we go.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.200
-♪ Popular mathematics ♪

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.968
♪ Mathematics ♪

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.334
-This is new?
A new segment?

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.834
-It's new to some -- some eyes.
-Okay, sure.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.868
-Let's take a look
at our first equation here.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.868
If you take Shrek...
-Yeah.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.834
-...okay, plus a Peloton...
-Yeah.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.801
-...it equals
the Jolly Green Giant.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.834
Are you understanding?
-No.

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:38.567
-You're not understanding.
Yeah, I'll give you another one.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:39.834
I'll give you another example.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.901
You take a Labradoodle...
-Yeah.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.868
-...plus an electric razor,

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.734
it equals Rand Paul.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:49.400
Are you understanding math?
-Not yet.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.567
-Yeah, I'm trying
to help you out.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:51.734
Let me give you another example.

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:55.567
If you take "Wheel of Fortune"
minus the wheel,

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.667
minus Vanna White,
minus Pat Sajak,

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.334
minus the audience, plus Wi-Fi,

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.834
it equals Wordle.

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:05.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.634
-Ohhh!

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:08.400
-Let me --
Here's another example.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.267
If you take high school
minus homework plus ecstasy,

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.901
it equals "Euphoria."

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.400
-Oh.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.701
Okay.
-You understand.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.667
-That I understand.
-That one, you --

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:23.000
If you take Shaq...
-Shaq.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.133
-...plus Kevin Hart,

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:28.067
plus telling the dentist
you floss every single day,

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:30.167
it equals "Big Little Lies."

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.067
Here's another one.
You'll get this one.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:40.033
-Maybe.
-Chris Evans plus Tina Fey

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.801
plus getting something
off a high shelf

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.801
equals Christina Ricci.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:47.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:50.234
♪♪

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:52.634
-Christina reaching.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:56.367
If you take Christmas
minus decorations, minus fun,

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:59.200
plus overpriced candy
equals Valentine's Day.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:06.067
My jam's Whitman's Sampler.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:08.400
-Ooh, yeah.
-That's my jam right there.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.267
'Cause then you do all the thing
and the candies are all good,

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.334
